[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Project foundations that maintain control
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Regulatory bodies that oversee implementations
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 2. **Immutability limitations** — Blockchains are theoretically immutable but have experienced:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Hard forks (e.g., Ethereum's DAO hack reversal)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - 51% attacks on some networks
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Practical reversibility under certain conditions
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 3. **Scalability omitted** — The summary doesn't mention ongoing challenges with transaction speed and energy consumption
