[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Security level** | Security depends on consensus mechanism, network size, and cryptography. Not all blockchains are equally secure. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Immutability limits** | A 51% attack could theoretically alter records; smaller/less distributed chains are more vulnerable. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Transaction speed** | Decentralization often creates trade-offs with transaction speed compared to centralized systems. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Transparency scope** | Bitcoin is pseudonymous, not fully anonymous; Ethereum's smart contracts aren't always transparent in behavior. |
