[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 2. **"Revolutionary"** - While promising, quantum computing remains in early stages:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Current devices are "NISQ" (Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum) with limited qubits and high error rates
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Practical applications beyond demonstrations remain largely theoretical
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Timeline for practical impact is uncertain
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 3. **Missing important limitations**:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Quantum decoherence and error rates are major obstacles
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Quantum advantage requires specific problem structures
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m    - Scaling to useful numbers of qubits remains unsolved
