[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61089, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - The summary implies broad applicability when quantum advantage is actually limited to particular problem types (e.g., integer factorization, database searching, simulating quantum systems)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61089, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Readers are left without understanding the *actual scope* of quantum computing's utility
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61089, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Claims like "drug discovery" and "optimization" are vague—many optimization problems don't have proven quantum advantages
