[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64308, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m Nanotechnology manipulates matter at the atomic and molecular scale (1-100 nanometers) to create practical applications—such as iron oxide nanoparticles used in medical imaging, carbon nanotubes in composite materials, and experimental targeted drug delivery systems—though most clinical and commercial uses remain in early stages compared to their theoretical potential.
