[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - **Control systems**: Fairly states that sophisticated systems execute driving functions
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - **Potential benefits**: The promised benefits are widely cited in industry and research:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m   - **Safety improvements**: Supported by claims that human error causes ~94% of accidents
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m   - **Reduced congestion**: Theoretically possible through optimized routing and platooning
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m   - **Mobility access**: Valid for elderly, disabled, and vision-impaired populations
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m ## Claims Requiring Context ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | Claim | Qualification |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | "Improve road safety" | Depends on deployment context; limited real-world data exist. Safety varies significantly by conditions (weather, urban vs. highway) |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | "Reduce traffic congestion" | Speculative; could increase vehicle miles traveled ("induced demand") |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60085, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | "Without human intervention" | Most current vehicles (SAE Level 2-3) still require human oversight; true Level 5 autonomy remains unrealized |
