[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 2. **Practical limitations**: Current quantum computers are:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Prone to errors and decoherence
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Limited in qubit count
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Require extreme cooling (near absolute zero)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Far from solving real-world problems at scale
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 3. **"Exponential speedup" qualified**: This applies to particular algorithms (like Shor's for factoring), not quantum computing generally.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
