[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Claims Requiring Nuance ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 1. **"Clean energy sources"** - Mostly accurate, but with caveats:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Solar and wind are very clean during operation
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Hydroelectric can have environmental impacts (ecosystem disruption, methane from reservoirs)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Manufacturing panels/turbines has environmental costs
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 2. **Implied universality** - The passage doesn't mention:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Geothermal and biomass as other renewable sources
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - That "renewable" doesn't always mean "zero-impact"
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Geographic limitations (wind/solar depend on location)
