[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Important Caveats & Nuances ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ### 1. **"Safely" Requires Context**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - No autonomous vehicle is yet proven to be safer than human drivers in all conditions
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Safety varies significantly by manufacturer, testing conditions, and weather scenarios
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Unverified claim**: The implicit assumption that current AVs operate "safely" universally
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ### 2. **"Independently" Has Limitations**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Most deployed AVs operate in **geofenced areas** (limited geographic zones)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Many require remote human operators for edge cases or failures
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Only Level 4-5 autonomy can truly operate without driver intervention; most current vehicles are Level 2-3
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ### 3. **Missing Critical Elements**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - V2V/V2X communication (vehicle-to-vehicle data sharing)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Cybersecurity infrastructure
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Fail-safe redundancy systems
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64574, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Regulatory frameworks (jurisdiction-dependent)
