[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64834, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - **"Resistant to fraud"**: Nuanced claim. Blockchain prevents certain types of fraud (double-spending, retroactive changes) but doesn't eliminate all fraud risks (e.g., social engineering, 51% attacks on smaller networks, compromised private keys).
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64834, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - **Universal transparency**: Not all blockchains are equally transparent. Private/permissioned blockchains restrict visibility.
