[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59864, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m Gene editing technologies like CRISPR enable scientists to make precise changes to DNA sequences in living organisms. These tools have significant potential applications in treating genetic diseases, improving crops, and advancing medical research, though they also raise ethical questions about their use and long-term effects.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m # Weakness of This Summary
