[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The summary uses vague, general language ("scientific discovery," "technological advancement," "humanity's understanding") without providing any concrete illustrations of what these mean in practice. A reader gains no sense of *what* has actually been discovered, *which* technologies have advanced, or *how* our understanding has changed. Adding specific examples—such as the discovery of exoplanets, development of satellite technology, or evidence about the Big Bang—would make the summary more informative and meaningful.
