[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - It doesn't mention that quantum computers are still largely experimental and impractical for most real-world applications today
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - It omits discussion of **decoherence** and **error rates**—major obstacles that severely limit current quantum computers' reliability and scalability
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - It implies quantum computers are broadly superior without clarifying they're only advantageous for *specific problem types*, not general computing tasks
