[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Current quantum computers (NISQ era) are small-scale and noisy
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - No practical quantum advantage has been demonstrated for real-world business problems yet
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Most existing systems have high error rates requiring error correction
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 3. **Cryptography clarification** — Potentially misleading:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - Quantum computers could *break* current encryption (threat)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61637, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m    - They could also *enable* new quantum-safe encryption (opportunity)
