[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Current accessibility** - Quantum computers remain experimental and inaccessible to most users/organizations
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Limited applicability** - Despite the "exponential speedup" claim, quantum advantages only apply to specific problem types; they won't revolutionize general computing tasks
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Scalability challenges** - Current systems have far too few stable qubits to tackle most real-world problems
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The summary creates an overly optimistic impression by emphasizing potential without noting that practical, widely-applicable quantum computers remain years or decades away. This is misleading for readers seeking a balanced understanding.
