[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Privacy coins and private blockchains address different needs
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Security depends heavily on the specific implementation and consensus mechanism
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **"Resistant to tampering"** — More precisely:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Computationally difficult, not impossible
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - A 51% attack could theoretically alter records
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Immutability is practical, not absolute
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **"Eliminating the need for central authority"** — Depends on use case:
