[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Distributed ledger technology**: Correctly describes blockchain's foundational architecture
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Multiple computers/nodes**: Accurate—transactions are stored across a network
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Resistance to tampering**: Valid—cryptographic hashing and consensus mechanisms make alterations extremely difficult to execute undetected
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Permanent linking**: Correct—blocks reference previous blocks via cryptographic hashes
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Immutable chain**: Generally accurate—changing past records would require recalculating all subsequent blocks, which is computationally prohibitive
