[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ## Nuances & Clarifications ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | Point | Clarification |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m |-------|--------------|
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **"No single entity can control"** | Partially true but requires context: Centralized blockchains (private chains) *can* be controlled by entities; only truly decentralized networks resist single-entity control |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **"Permanently linked"** | More precisely: cryptographically linked through hash functions, not physically linked |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **"Resistant to fraud"** | Better stated as "resistant to certain types of fraud"—smart contract bugs, 51% attacks, and social engineering remain vulnerabilities |
