[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Accurate Claims ✓
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Distributed ledger technology**: Correctly describes blockchain's fundamental architecture
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Securely records transactions**: Accurate - uses cryptographic hashing and digital signatures
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Multiple computers**: Correct - blockchain operates across a network of nodes
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Transparent**: Valid - transaction history is visible to network participants
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Immutable**: Accurate - past blocks cannot be altered without detection due to cryptographic linking
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Decentralized**: Correct - no single authority controls the ledger
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Tamper-proof**: Accurate - cryptographic mechanisms prevent undetected modifications
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Verifiable**: Correct - participants can independently verify transactions and the ledger state
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Minor Clarifications
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Immutability scope** | More precisely: extremely difficult to alter without detection, rather than absolutely immutable. A 51% attack could theoretically alter historical records. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Transparency limits** | Some blockchains (private/permissioned) restrict visibility; this summary assumes public blockchains. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Verification scope** | Verification depends on network consensus rules; not all claims on a blockchain are inherently "true," only that they were recorded. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
