[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64575, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64575, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m The summary doesn't clarify what "nanoscale" actually means (typically 1-100 nanometers) or distinguish between theoretical concepts, laboratory research, and commercially available nanotechnology products. This leaves readers uncertain about how mature or practical these applications actually are. For example, while targeted drug delivery is mentioned as an application, most such therapies are still in development rather than widely available treatments. A stronger summary would indicate the difference between promising research and established technology.
