[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m ## Important Nuances to Consider
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m | **Security level** | While resistant to tampering, blockchain is not *completely* immune—attacks like 51% attacks are theoretically possible on some networks |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m | **Transparency vs. Privacy** | "Transparent" can be misleading; transactions are visible but identities may be pseudonymous, not necessarily private or publicly linked to individuals |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m | **Fraud prevention** | Blockchains prevent certain types of fraud (double-spending) but don't eliminate all fraud risks (e.g., social engineering, smart contract bugs) |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m | **Verification burden** | While verifiable in theory, most users don't actually verify transactions; they rely on network participants |
