[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Important Clarifications & Nuances
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m **⚠️ Needs Context:**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 1. **"Exponentially faster"** - This is partially true but requires qualification:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Quantum advantage is *problem-specific*, not universal
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Not all problems benefit from quantum speedup
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Some problems show polynomial rather than exponential speedup
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Classical algorithms may also improve
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 2. **Missing context on limitations:**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Quantum computers are not faster at *all* tasks
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Decoherence and error rates remain significant challenges
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Current quantum computers are still in early stages (NISQ era - Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m    - Practical quantum computers require extreme conditions (near absolute zero temperatures)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
