[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62484, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m This creates an overly optimistic impression that autonomous vehicles are a solved problem, when significant technical and regulatory hurdles remain unresolved. A more balanced summary would note that while the *technology exists*, widespread safe deployment still faces major challenges.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m **Lack of specificity about which problems quantum computers actually excel at:**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m The summary claims quantum computers solve "certain complex problems exponentially faster" but doesn't explain *which* problems or *why*. This is misleading because:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
