[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Distributed ledger technology**: Correctly describes blockchain's core architecture
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Records transactions across multiple computers**: Accurate description of how data is replicated across nodes
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Transparency**: Valid characteristic—participants can view the ledger
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Decentralized approach**: Accurately reflects the elimination of central intermediaries
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Immutability**: Correct—altering past records requires prohibitive computational effort
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"Extremely difficult for data to be altered"** — This needs qualification:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - True for established blockchains with significant computational power (like Bitcoin)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Less secure for smaller or newer blockchains with fewer nodes
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Also depends on consensus mechanism (Proof of Work vs. Proof of Stake differences)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"Eliminates need for central authority"** — Partially true but context-dependent:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - True for *validating* transactions, but doesn't eliminate all authority
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Private blockchains still require governance structures
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Some centralization of decision-making typically remains (e.g., protocol upgrades)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ## Missing Important Caveats
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60915, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
