[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Qubits as fundamental units**: Correct—qubits are the quantum equivalent of classical bits
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Superposition principle**: Accurate—qubits can exist in multiple states simultaneously until measured
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Parallel processing capability**: Valid—superposition does enable processing multiple possibilities concurrently
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Application areas mentioned**: All are legitimate areas of quantum research (cryptography, drug discovery, optimization)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ## Nuances & Caveats ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **1. "Exponentially faster" — Partially verified but needs context**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Quantum computers offer **exponential speedup for specific problem classes** (e.g., factoring via Shor's algorithm, certain optimization problems)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - They don't automatically solve all problems faster—many tasks show no quantum advantage
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Speedup is problem-dependent, not universal
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **2. Cryptography claim — Requires clarification**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Quantum computers could **break** certain cryptographic systems (RSA, ECC)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - They could also **enable** new quantum-secure cryptography
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Statement is ambiguous as written
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **3. Current limitations not mentioned**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Quantum decoherence and error rates remain major obstacles
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Current quantum computers (NISQ era) have limited practical applications
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Scalability to useful problem sizes is still largely theoretical
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
