[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=61089, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m Cybersecurity is the practice of defending computer systems and networks against malicious digital attacks and unauthorized access to sensitive data. It employs various technical, administrative, and physical measures to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of information.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65589, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m # Revised Summary
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65589, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65589, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m Nanotechnology involves engineering materials and devices at the molecular and atomic level (1-100 nanometers) to create enhanced or unique properties, with promising applications in drug delivery, diagnostics, materials science, and electronics, though widespread adoption remains limited by manufacturing costs, regulatory uncertainties, and the fact that many applications are still in development phases.
