[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60913, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The overview is **substantially accurate but optimistically framed**, reflecting early-stage technology potential rather than current widespread impact.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m **Lack of discussion of ethical concerns and limitations:**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m The summary presents gene editing in an entirely positive light without acknowledging significant controversies and practical challenges, such as:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Off-target effects (unintended mutations elsewhere in the genome)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Ethical debates around germline editing (heritable changes)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Equity issues in access to gene therapies
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59863, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Regulatory uncertainties
