[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Distributed ledger technology**: Correct. Blockchain maintains copies of data across multiple networked computers.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Secure record-keeping**: Verified. Uses cryptographic hashing and digital signatures to protect data integrity.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Difficult to alter past records**: Accurate. The chain-linking of blocks and consensus mechanisms make retroactive changes computationally impractical.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Decentralized approach**: Correct. Removes reliance on single points of failure or control.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=64065, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Peer-to-peer transactions**: Verified. Blockchain enables direct transactions between parties without intermediaries.
