[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - Quantum computers today have high error rates requiring extensive error correction
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - This overhead could eliminate theoretical advantages for near-term devices
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - We're still in early experimental stages; practical advantages remain largely theoretical
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m **"Cryptography" needs context:**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - Quantum computers would *break* current encryption (threat)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - But also enable *new* quantum-secure cryptography (opportunity)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60699, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m - The framing matters significantly
