[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=59865, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m Quantum computers leverage qubits that exist in superposition—simultaneously representing 0 and 1—enabling them to process vast solution spaces in parallel. This fundamental advantage allows quantum computers to solve certain complex problems exponentially faster than classical computers, particularly in cryptography, optimization, and drug discovery.
