[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ## ⚠️ Minor Qualifications Needed
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"Resistant to fraud"** - More precisely: resistant to *certain types* of fraud. Blockchain doesn't prevent all fraud (e.g., user error, social engineering, 51% attacks on smaller networks)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"No single entity controls the data"** - True for public blockchains, but *private/permissioned blockchains* may have centralized control
