[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | Claim | Consideration |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m |-------|---------------|
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **"Ensures transparency"** | Transparency varies—Bitcoin is pseudonymous (not anonymous), Monero prioritizes privacy. Not all blockchains are equally transparent. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **"Prevents tampering"** | More accurately: makes tampering extremely costly and detectable, but not absolutely impossible (e.g., 51% attacks on smaller networks). |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65588, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **"No single entity can control"** | True for decentralized networks, but not for private/permissioned blockchains (Hyperledger, etc.) where entities do have control. |
