[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ### Levels of Autonomy
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The definition doesn't specify that autonomy exists on a spectrum. Most vehicles today are **Level 2-3** (partial automation), not fully autonomous. Only a few operate at **Level 4-5** (full autonomy in defined/all conditions).
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ### Decision-Making Complexity
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The phrase "make driving decisions independently" may oversimplify—these systems follow programmed algorithms and rules rather than truly independent decision-making.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ### Real-World Limitations
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m The definition implies more capability than currently exists:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Most AVs still require human oversight in complex conditions
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Geographic/weather limitations remain significant
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Edge cases (unusual scenarios) still challenge current technology
