[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Important Nuances & Caveats
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | Aspect | Clarification |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m |--------|---------------|
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Limited advantage scope** | Quantum speedup only applies to specific problem classes (factoring, optimization, simulation). Most everyday computing tasks won't benefit. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Decoherence challenges** | Qubits are fragile—superposition collapses easily due to environmental interference, making error correction critical |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Current state** | We're in the NISQ era (Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum)—current devices have 100-1000 qubits but high error rates |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m | **Not a universal speedup** | Quantum computers aren't simply "faster versions" of classical computers; they require fundamentally different algorithms |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=62380, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
