[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m **"Eliminates the need for a central authority"**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - *Accurate for*: Permission-less blockchains (Bitcoin, Ethereum) where no single entity controls validation
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - *Less accurate for*: Private/permissioned blockchains where organizations still control node access
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - *Clarification needed*: Authority is replaced by **consensus mechanisms** and cryptography, not eliminated entirely
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m **"Securely records transactions"**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - *True for*: Preventing tampering with recorded data
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m - *Important limitation*: Security depends heavily on the specific implementation, consensus mechanism, and network security
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60945, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
