[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **Scope limitation** | Quantum advantage isn't universal—most everyday computing tasks won't benefit. Speed gains are problem-specific. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **Decoherence challenge** | Summary doesn't mention that superposition is fragile; environmental interference causes qubits to lose quantum properties. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **Current state** | Existing quantum computers are still in early stages (NISQ era—Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum). Practical applications remain limited. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65111, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m | **Error rates** | Quantum computers currently have high error rates, requiring quantum error correction (not mentioned). |
