[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"Vast computational spaces in parallel"**: Partially accurate but needs clarification. Quantum computers don't process all possibilities equally—they use interference to amplify correct answers and cancel incorrect ones. This is more sophisticated than simple parallel exploration.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **"Solve certain complex problems exponentially faster"**: Accurate but should note this applies to *specific* problem types (factoring, database search, optimization). Most problems don't show quantum advantage.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67506, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
