[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Distributed ledger technology**: Correct. Blockchain maintains copies of transaction records across multiple nodes.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Records transactions**: Accurate. This is a primary function of blockchain systems.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Decentralized approach**: True. Blockchain operates without a central authority controlling the network.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Difficulty in altering data**: Valid. The cryptographic linking of blocks and consensus mechanisms make retroactive changes computationally expensive.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65109, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Changes require verification**: Correct. Most blockchains use consensus protocols (Proof of Work, Proof of Stake, etc.) to validate transactions.
