[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60913, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 2. **"Multiple possibilities simultaneously"**: While conceptually useful, this phrasing can mislead. Quantum computers don't truly "try all possibilities at once"—they manipulate probability amplitudes in ways classical computers cannot easily replicate.
