[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=67427, ip=10.0.10.50)[0m Quantum computers harness qubits in superposition to potentially solve specific complex problems—like factoring and optimization—exponentially faster than classical computers, though current systems remain experimental due to technical barriers like high error rates and scalability limitations, with practical advantages still largely theoretical outside specialized domains.
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
