[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m ## Nuances and Limitations to Consider ⚠️
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | **"Exponentially faster"** | Partially qualified—quantum speedup is *problem-dependent*. Not all problems benefit equally. Some show polynomial or no advantage. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | **Current state** | The summary doesn't mention that practical quantum advantage remains limited; most quantum computers are still in research/early development phases. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | **Decoherence** | Omits a critical challenge: qubits lose superposition quickly, limiting computation time. |
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=65748, ip=10.0.10.175)[0m | **Error rates** | Current quantum computers have high error rates, requiring error correction that adds significant overhead. |
