[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **"Securely and transparently"**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Transparency**: ✓ Most blockchains are transparent (transactions are visible to network participants)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - **Security**: ⚠️ Nuance needed—security depends heavily on:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - The specific consensus mechanism (Proof of Work vs. Proof of Stake, etc.)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Implementation quality
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Network size and participation
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m   - Not all blockchains guarantee equal security levels
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m **"Prevents unauthorized alterations"**
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - ⚠️ More precisely: Makes unauthorized alterations extremely difficult and detectable
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Technically possible to alter past records if someone controls >50% of network power (51% attack)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m - Immutability is probabilistic, not absolute
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=60912, ip=10.0.10.142)[0m ## Omissions
