[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ## Unverified/Overstated Claims
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ⚠ **"Unprecedented accuracy"** - Needs clarification:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - CRISPR has *off-target effects* (edits unintended DNA sequences) at measurable rates
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Accuracy varies by target and delivery method
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Better accuracy than older tools ≠ perfectly accurate
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m ⚠ **"Revolutionary potential"** - Vague qualifier:
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Some applications are proven (certain blood disorders in clinical trials)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Many applications remain experimental or theoretical
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - Clinical translation has been slower than early hype suggested
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Regulatory status**: Only limited CRISPR therapies approved; most are still in development
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Challenges**: Delivery to cells, immune responses, ethical concerns (germline editing)
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Cost and accessibility**: Remains expensive and unavailable in most settings
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m - **Ethical concerns**: Germline/heritable editing remains highly controversial
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m 
[36m(_strands_fanout_task pid=66584, ip=10.0.10.235)[0m The summary captures real scientific potential but oversimplifies by omitting current limitations and regulatory reality.
